NOTES ON SCOPE
==============

This is the licence Slackware itself uses for its build scripts, chosen
deliberately: this is a Slackware port, and its scripts sit alongside stock
ones that carry the same terms.

It covers the original work in this tree -- the SlackBuilds, the tooling under
tools/, the installer text under installer-text/, and the documentation.

It does NOT relicense anything this tree merely carries or builds:

  * The Linux kernel, U-Boot, m1n1, Mesa, PipeWire and every other upstream
    project retain their own licences. Building or patching software does not
    change its terms.

  * The patches this tree originates are offered under the licence of the
    project each one changes: those under source/kernel_armv8-mac/patches/
    are GPL-2.0, as kernel code is; those for asahi-fwextract and
    asahi-scripts are MIT, as those projects are. See NOTICE.

  * The U-Boot series in source/hwm-bw-mac/patches/, the speakersafetyd
    patch and the tiny-dfr patch are other people's work, carried verbatim
    and under their own terms. Author and Signed-off-by lines are part of those files and are
    left intact. See NOTICE.

  * source/slackware-k/ is inherited from Slackware ARM and carries its own
    copyright notice, which is left untouched.

  * Some SlackBuilds here derive from Slackware's own -- notably mesa-asahi
    and pipewire-lv2, which take their meson flag sets from Slackware's.
    Those files retain the upstream copyright notices as well as this one,
    which is precisely what condition 1 above requires.


